abstract: >-
  Technical report on porting DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (552B mixture-of-experts, 189 GiB n-gram
  memory) to a llama.cpp fork and running it on a single RTX 5090 (31.8 GiB of VRAM) with
  125.7 GiB of RAM, with the routed experts streaming from NVMe: correctness against the
  reference implementation at its own fp8 rounding floor, 5.1 tokens/s on new content and
  21 tokens/s on resident content, a measured decomposition of the token into compute, PCIe
  and NVMe, the ceilings that follow, and the negative results (prefetch oracle, block
  verification, n-gram and DSpark drafts, encoder-only prefill). Includes the measurement
  tools and the raw results.
